# Generated by theming/apply-theme.py — don't hand-edit, edit the
# palette TOML instead and re-run apply-theme.py.
#
# Primary bg/fg/accent roles come straight from the palette (BackgroundNormal/
# Alternate -> bg, ForegroundNormal -> fg, DecorationFocus/Hover +
# ForegroundActive -> accent). Secondary semantic colors (link/negative/
# neutral/positive/inactive/visited) are two static sets picked by the
# palette's `mode` (light/dark) in apply-theme.py, not derived per-palette --
# same "proportionate effort" call already made elsewhere, just made
# mode-aware after the original single dark-tuned set turned out unreadable
# against a light palette's background (found via Catppuccin Latte, 2026-09-07).
